yesterday during the press briefing of  a white house press secretary jenn saki  there was a clarification about joe  biden's tax plan when joe biden said  nobody earning under thousand  dollars a year we'll see an increase in  taxes  did joe biden mean individuals earning  up to 400k  or did joe biden mean households earning  up to 400k  during yesterday's press briefing gen  saki clarified  that it means households that is  different  than four hundred thousand dollars per  person it's four hundred thousand  dollars  per household and within moments on fox  news  right-wing host charles payne as well as  republican senator chuck grassley  were saying look look we told you  joe biden is coming for middle  income people take a look at this clip  so then what if we go the exact  opposite way we know taxes were promised  and elections have consequences but i  don't think anyone thought  that the president president biden was  talking about  a household making four hundred thousand  i always tell people senator  be careful when you pick up your  torching and pitchforks sooner or later  you might end up in front of your own  house  the middle income people of this country  are smart enough to know that when they  hear a politician  or even the president united states say  that only high  income people the very wealthiest are  going to pay the tax  they know better if you go  there you're going to eventually end up  paying  taxing middle-income people so there are  two relevant parts here  first is is 400 000  as a household income is that middle  income  that's the first question the second  question is  are these the folks we should be  targeting for higher taxes so  when you say 400 000 for a household  that could be two people making 200k  each that could be someone makes 175 and  someone makes 25  could be you know 350 and 50. total 400  000 that puts you in the top two percent  of households in the united states so by  definition you're not in the middle  if you're in the top two percent now you  could say well  you're in the middle like you know you  anything that goes down to the second  percentile  and up to the 98th counts as middle and  then you've got  two percent of people that are poor and  two percent of people that are rich  i don't think most people would imagine  that the meat of the curve  is the middle 98 for example or the  middle  96 percent by definition if you're in  the top two percent you're not in the  middle income now you can go and look at  this for yourself if you go to dqydj.com  you can type in any household income if  you type in 400 000 for example  you will see you're in the 98th  percentile the top to get into the top  two percent this is 2019 data  to get into the top two percent you had  to make as a household  387 000 it's a little higher now  probably because of inflation  it's right around 400 000 a year puts  you in the top two percent  now the second part is actually more  interesting to me  you can like they're they're just wrong  that 400k is middle income you're in the  top two percent  the more interesting part is you can  absolutely make the case that we should  be targeting  not people who as individuals might only  make two hundred thousand  as part of a four hundred thousand  dollar household you should be looking  at people that are making five million a  year  20 million a year 200 million a year the  billionaires that there's  so much more meat on the bone there  that you shouldn't even include 400 000  households right now now that is a valid  argument in the sense that  you're not denying reality you're not  saying 400k is middle income now 400k is  still in the top  two percent but you should be targeting  the top one percent or the top  0.5 percent or the top 0.2 percent  400 000 is a lot of money in any city  but four hundred thousand in manhattan  with three kids  is nowhere near the same as four hundred  thousand dollars as a couple with no  kids in alabama  so you just open this up to more debate  potentially  if you make this about 10 million a year  and up or 20 million a year and up  there's no debate  in any city maybe if you have a thousand  kids right but but in any city with one  two three four kids  that's a ton of money anywhere maybe you  start there  and that is a different discussion and  one that certainly could be had but  there is no way to say  biden's coming for the middle class  by starting tax increases at 400 000  it's it's just look at a bell curve it's  not the case  um and and by the way there's one other  hypocrisy here  charles payne and chuck grassley talking  about  middle-income people making 400 000  but a 15 minimum wage is too much  that's just another level of how  everything is just political posturing  none of this is  none of this is honest or they're really  that dumb  you you decide which it is i think that  it's that they're not honest  we'll have more coverage of this on our  instagram  at david pakman show and find my latest  pastry haul by following me  on instagram david.pacman  today's show is sponsored by an  excellent audiobook  called takeover how a conservative  student club  captured the supreme court this is the  latest audiobook from noah feldman it  just came out  and a feldman actually narrates the  audiobook himself  noah feldman of course is a harvard law  professor and constitutional  scholar you may remember him from his  prominent role in trump's impeachment  number one  and the book takeover looks at how the  federalist society became the most  powerful legal organization in the  country  six of the nine current supreme court  justices  are current or former members of the  federalist society  and takeover dives into what the  organization is what it stands for  its relationship with american politics  the federalist  society is an organization anyone in my  audience  should be aware of and the audiobook has  a ton of excellent insight into it and  the role it plays  i really enjoyed listening to the  audiobook i think anybody  in my audience would as well so grab  takeover by noah feldman the audiobook  is just 4.99  and you can get it at davidpakman.com  takeover or wherever you buy audiobooks
 

